{
  "_doc": "Registry accumulator over the four devices of keys.json, committed in three epochs: device 0; devices 1 and 2 together; device 3. Register parks a PoP-verified key as pending; CommitEpoch sorts the pending keys by key_hash = blake3(pubkey48) ascending (bytewise) and appends them, index = append position. BMT (lib/bmt): key = key_hash, value = BE8(index); leaf_bytes = 0x4C || key_hash || BE8(index); leaf_hash = blake3(0x00 || leaf_bytes); internal = blake3(left32 || right32); path = key_hash bits MSB first; empty child = 32 zero bytes; a lone leaf in a subtree is that subtree's hash (no extension nodes), two leaves sharing a prefix get a chain of internals with zero siblings. Every root here was also recomputed from that rule alone. export_committed = ExportCommitted(): magic 0x4d565253 BE4 || version 0x01 || count BE4 || count x (pubkey48 || pop96 || active u8 || lastSeenMs BE8). CommitEpoch stamps lastSeenMs with the node's wall clock (so snapshots differ between nodes); the fixture overwrote it with commit_last_seen_ms. register/health = exact status and body of the gov5 handlers (pending: {committed:false,index:0}; committed: the index). health 'accumulator' is the root with 0x, all zeros when empty.",
